{% comment %}
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  BACKDROPSOURCE — EVENT SPONSORSHIP SPECIALISTS  (Shopify 2.0 section)
  File: sections/sponsorship-specialists.liquid
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Faithful, fully Theme-Editor-driven conversion of the
  "Event Sponsorship Specialists" landing wireframe.

  SECTIONS
  - Fixed top nav (transparent → solid on scroll)
  - Full-height HERO with rotating slide backgrounds, captions,
    dual CTAs, stat strip, dot nav + progress bar
  - Scrolling TICKER
  - About / Our story
  - Why event branding works (dark, stat cards)
  - Events portfolio (logo wall)
  - Who we help (Sponsors vs Organisers)
  - Testimonials (dark)
  - Final CTA  ·  optional in-page footer
  - Dual-role LEAD MODAL (Sponsor / Organiser) → Google Sheet

  HEADER / HERO COLLAPSE FIX
  - This page renders its OWN fixed nav over a 100vh hero. To stop the
    theme's own fixed/sticky header stacking on top of it (the "collapse"),
    "Hide the store's main header on this page" is ON by default. Turn it
    off if you'd rather keep the theme header (then also hide the in-page
    nav, or set the hero top offset).

  PERFORMANCE
  - Inline SVG icons (no icon-font CDN). One Google-Fonts request.
  - CSS scoped to .bds-spec, JS scoped to {{ section.id }}.
  - Hero slides: first image eager, the rest lazy. width/height on imgs.

  LEAD FORM (fully self-contained — no external theme assets)
  - "Become a Sponsor" / "I'm an Organiser" open one modal with
    role-specific fields + optional file upload.
  - Validation is built in: email format + typo + disposable block +
    live MX deliverability (dns.google); international phone with flag +
    dial code auto-set by IP (ipapi.co → api.country.is) and validated
    via libphonenumber-js (lazy CDN, length fallback). India default.
  - Posts (fetch, no-cors, URLSearchParams) to the "Lead form endpoint"
    Apps Script Web App. Sponsor → "Sponsors" tab, Organiser → "Event
    Owners" tab. Files sent as file_base64/file_name/file_type.
  ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
{% endcomment %}

